    "narrative_title": "Global diesel supply shock and political responses",
    "narrative_summary": "A sudden squeeze in diesel availability — driven by export curbs (notably Russia), refinery/market strains and rising demand — has created a global price spike that is triggering urgent political interventions. National governments and the G7 are using strategic-reserve releases, threatened export bans and tax/trade measures as control levers, producing reinforcing and balancing feedbacks between markets, diplomacy and domestic politics (including U.S. midterm timing). The system is open: external shocks (war, sanctions, production decisions) and policy actions feed into prices and trade flows, which in turn reshape political incentives and further policy moves.",
    "scope": "Physical diesel supply chain (refining, inventories, shipping, trade flows), diesel prices and downstream inflation effects, national strategic reserves and policy levers (export bans, stock releases, taxes/duties), principal state and industry actors directly engaged (U.S., EU/G7, Russia, refiners, major retailers).",
    "super_system": "The global oil and refined-products market embedded in international energy security and geopolitics.",
    "adjacent_subsystems": [
      "EU energy security and internal political coordination",
      "U.S. domestic politics and trade policy (midterms)",
      "Russian export policy and sanctions regime",
      "Emerging markets' fuel markets and industrial supply chains (e.g., India)"
    ],
    "evidence_headlines": [
      "Trump 'thinking about' diesel export ban, but says it could have 'negative impact' on gasoline",
      "G-7 Agrees to Release 100 Million Barrels of Diesel and Crude",
      "Russia extends diesel export ban",
      "EU countries in crisis talks over release of diesel stocks",
      "EXCLUSIVE: US tells France and Germany to release diesel stocks or face US export ban, sources say",
      "Europe’s leaders rush to release diesel from stockpiles as fuel-shock hangs over U.S. midterms"
    ]
  },
